# Fishing rod + 5000-size spinning reel. Generated by emit_toml.py --
# edit blockout.py / rod_spec.py, never this file.
#
# The blank is a CHAIN: Butt -> S1 -> ... -> S24, each node's origin
# at its own base, each mesh running up +Y from there. A bend is
# rot_euler [pitch, 0, 0] on S1..S24 and EVERY JOINT TAKES THE SAME
# ANGLE (rod_spec._angles), so the fight script is one identical line
# on all 24 of them: pitch = 0.2917 + 4.2917 * stress / 100.
# loom_ecs composes world = parent_world x local to any depth, so the
# 24 rotations make one curve. NEVER put a scale other than [1,1,1]
# on a chain node: compose()
# scales the local matrix's COLUMNS, so a parent's scale is applied after
# a child's rotation and shears it.
#
# Baked at stress 0. Fast action, 110 deg of tip angle at stress 100:
#   S1 4.6  S2 4.6  S3 4.6  S4 4.6  S5 4.6  S6 4.6  S7 4.6  S8 4.6  S9 4.6  S10 4.6  S11 4.6  S12 4.6  S13 4.6  S14 4.6  S15 4.6  S16 4.6  S17 4.6  S18 4.6  S19 4.6  S20 4.6  S21 4.6  S22 4.6  S23 4.6  S24 4.6

